Why don't anybody in this thread like this?
I think it is a TRULY GREAT IDEA!

It would be simpler, cleaner and neater than naming your speed boots 
"Stash on lvl 12" *or* using an external editor. There are NO balance 
issues, and it would add depth to the game (the wood nymph steals your 
notepad!). It could also make it easier to remember things when you want 
to post YAAP, and being a physical thing it would of course not be 
subject to amnesia.

Keeping game notes IN the game appeals to me. I often play remote, and 
from different locations, so to keep notes in a central location I would 
have to log in on the server twice to open an editor, escaping to a 
shell is just too much roundabout. With a notepad the notes would go 
where they should go, in the save-file. AND IT WOULD BE SOOO EASY to 
implement using current features... Applying the notebook would pop up a 
menu like e.g. applying bags does:

     Do what?

     a - Add a note
     r - Read notes
     b - Both of the above

Adding a note works exactly like E)ngrave, and viewing notes works 
exactly like "\"; no editing - just viewing. An optional "remove notes" 
feature could work by giving you an entry-by-entry selectable list like 
a bag inventory.

HAHA, a cursed notepad could be subject to "rubout" (like messing up an 
engraving) when you read it. A notepad may be subject to rubout on water 
and fire damage too, or maybe that would decrease its usefulness too 
much -- at least you should be able to fireproof and grease it, and a 
blessed notepad would be 90% unlikely to be affected.

Anyway, having 24 (and --more--, and --more--) one-liner notes 
immediately available (3 keyclicks: apply+<invnt>+read, or even better 
read+<invnt>) is not such a stupid idea, compared to the alternatives. 
And if you don't like it, just DON'T spend $10 on it at Rath Luirc's 
second-hand bookstore. I for one would go out of my way to obtain one, 
and I would keep it in the "a"-spot, to activate with a+a+a and r+a.

IN FACT, will the Dev-team let me join them if I send them a patch???

